cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KERN in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "KERN: a zero-trust L0-L5 verification gateway for machine-checked claims"
abstract: >-
  KERN admits a claim about code only when it is confirmed by a machine —
  an SMT solver, a formal proof, or a reproducible execution fact — and never
  because of text, documentation or a green CI. It ships a Zig 0.17 core with a
  native Z3 proof-DAG checker (independent re-verification of every solver
  step), Belnap B4 four-valued logic, Lean 4 proofs (0 errors, 0 sorry), a
  content-addressed .kimg container with Merkle integrity, contracts written as
  plain Python comments, a Model Context Protocol server for AI agents, and a
  can-fail harness that proves every check is capable of failing.
authors:
  - family-names: "Kalinousky"
    given-names: "Vital"
